# Constrained pairwise model of the kestrike configuration factors.
# Generate the rows with `pict model.pict > rows.tsv`: order two over the
# 23,040-combination product gives 21 rows with PICT built from commit
# ab76c2548f551fcb46314e58653a1bd1172f3a72, whose generation without `/r`
# is deterministic. The fault profile selects the link and media faults of
# each row's GET. The exact unit, clean-reserve and slot boundaries have
# their own probes. The factors are the activation envelope's inputs too:
# every row's owner starts on exactly its envelope share.
# A row's derived values (the clean reserve, the retired allowance, the
# headroom target, read commands, response buffers, peer shares, the
# per-peer GET reserve, the batch, the receive reserve and the PUT shape)
# follow from its factors; the GET reserve factor is the request slots PUTs
# leave to GETs, so the PUT caps derive within the slots and shares the two
# reserves leave. The global cap is the most PUTs whose structural floor
# under an allowance of one largest charge leaves a unit for the published
# object, so the volume units and the record sizes can lower the cap, down
# to zero. Validation bounds the headroom target by the volume's whole
# charges of the largest record's first extent; the smallest volume, 19
# units, lowers a 9-unit largest record's cap to zero and still holds its
# target in whole 9-unit charges beside a one-unit object. The retired
# allowance is every slot's largest charge, within half
# the units the clean reserve, the cap's largest charges and the published
# object leave, and at least one largest charge; the headroom target is the
# cap's structural floor under that allowance. Only a factor combination
# that no derived choice satisfies is
# constrained here. A command span below the record chunk length leaves the
# header windows and the receive-write buffer without a whole chunk, so a
# 16-KiB chunk needs a 16-KiB span.

VolumeUnits:      19, 63, 64, 65, 129
StorageSlots:     4, 16, 33
ChunkBytes:       4096, 8192, 16384
SpanBytes:        8192, 16384
Depth:            4, 8
RequestSlots:     2, 4
ReadAhead:        0, 1
Principals:       1, 2
GetReserve:       1, 2
BodyCap:          200, 32768
FaultProfile:     healthy, gray, error-omission, hostile-media

IF [ChunkBytes] = 16384 THEN [SpanBytes] = 16384;
